Thanks to this group I ascended another char, Comptril the Gomish
Ranger!

To recap my previous posts

Alter on dlvl1.  Ran through Soko and got the BoH.  Also became
invisible from a wand.  Acquired a / oTele and /oCanc as well and
identified them early on.

Back up to the mines.  A bunch of bones piles provided a CoMR, two
magic lamps, and other goddies.  Mine's End was Mimic of the Mines and
luckily got the luck stone (the other gray rock was in very difficult
to reach spot).

Back up to the alter on dlvl1.  Got that cool warhammer with lightning
bolts.

Down the main branch again got some wishes from a throne and one from
the extra magic lamp.  Got Silver dragon scale mail, gauntlets of
power.

Found another alter and got Magicbane with the first #offer. Came
across a cross-aligned temple and got naked AC down to 1.   Figured
out what a ?oID looked like.  Used about 7 blessed ?oID to ID most all
of my stuff.

Had some fun with the rubber chicken and Medusa's titan.  Killed
Medusa.  Got ready to move below her level.  Then while putting stuff
in my bag, I guess I accidentally hit / b/c next thing I knew all my
wands were going into the BoH.  And of course I still had the /oCanc.

*KABOOM*

All my scrolls and potions (lots of holy and unholy water) and wands,
my candles, my food, my magic markers -- all lost.

I came here for advice and got great help.

Next killed a Tengu and felt jumpy.   I remembered there was an extra
=oTC back at
the minetown temple.  Sent our hero to get that.  Did the quest
without much trouble.  Only
thing I really needed was a BoH.  Thinking there might be one in the
minetown shops, I got some mummy wrappings and headed back down
there.  Unfortunately no such luck.

So back to the main branch.  Kept thinking I might find the entrance
to the Fort, but vaults were very rare this game.

The Castle presented a problem since the bugle was in the exploding
bag.  Our hero did have a =oLev, but there were lots of ; in the moat
(and we've had too many YASD from them drowning our hero).  I thought
the silver bell might open the drawbridge, but apparently it has to be
blessed, which the holy water was also in the exploding bag.

So it was tedious but the Longbow of Diana killed all the ; in the
moat (I don't recommend levitating when shooting the bow).

In through the back door.  Guess what - tons of silver dragons (after
we wasted a wish on SDSM).  And yes one of them dropped scales.

There was a pair of buckled boots in one of the storerooms, just like
the pair we found in the statue of Perseus and lost in the exploding
bag.  Nothing else terribly interesting.

The castle wand was used for 2 blessed ?oCharging (got 1).  Had to
immediately recharge and then got a BoH.

There was another /oCanc in the barracks (yeah I shouldn't touch it,
but I did).
Filled the new BoH up with stuff and then it was down to the VotD.
Cleared the Valley without much trouble and soon was seeing the
message:

"You are standing at the gate to Gehennom.
Unspeakable cruelty and harm lurk down there.
Are you sure you want to enter? [yn] (n)"

Down we go.  After a brief fight with a purple L, it was time to get
more holy water.  So back up to all the stashes and put them in the
new BoH.  This took a lot longer than I expected.  But our hero ended
up with 20 potions of water ready for alter.

Next wish from the Castle Wand was a blessed magic marker.

Spent a lot of time using blessed ?oID and still had a bunch of unIDed
stuff.  But finially did figure out what ?oEA and?oEW looked like and
realized I had a "oLS and a =oFA!  With that knowledge, enchanted some
armor and big-M warhammer (in retrospect, choosing Magicbane for a
primary weapon and making ?oEA instead of ?oEW might have been the
better choice - eh but it worked out fine).

So with now AC:-26 it was off to Gehennom.  It turns out the first
level was Asmodeus' Lair.  Bribe him.   Only thing interesting on that
level was a runed broadsword named Orcrist.  Left it where we found
it.

Next level almost finished mapping it when, "You sense a faint wave of
psychic energy."  NO NO NO.  We had a ?oGeno in BoH.  Whip it out,
bless it, goodbye h's.

Exploration of Gehennom wasn't too interesting.  Never realized how
common elves and c's were in Gehennom.  Lots of collecting gold then
back up to buy protection from the priest in VotD.  Eventually I set
up a chest next to the alter to contain my ever growing stash (after
the BoH explosion I figured I'd never have enough stuff to stash again
- boy was I wrong).

My biggest concern at this point was that I was only Xp:15 with less
than 150hp.  Again usually I'm close to Xp:30 with 400+hp but I guess
just wizards have to buff up that much to survive.

Accidentally fell through a hole and ended up in Juiblex' Swamp was on
dlvl35.  I didn't get the " It looks rather muddy down here." message
until after I had wandered around for a bit.

Not wanting to fight him, I quickly found the upstairs and climbed up
to dlvl34 where Baalzebub was waiting for me.  Sheesh.  I stashed most
of my gold in the bag and then bribed him with what I had visible.

Cleared that and back to Juiblex.  I don't understand it.  Sometimes
Juiblex is as hard to kill as Big-Y or Big-D, but sometimes he's like
this.  Dies after one or two hits.  Then spent some time using the
longbow to kill some things in the water (don't want them catching me
on the ascension run or something).

Did some nurse dancing on dlvl36.  Got two whole hp.  I killed it for
that incompetence.  In fact I would kill them all from this point on.
If you're going to make me take my clothes off, I better get something
good for it.

Found the stairs to Vlad's tower on dlvl39.  On the first level of the
tower was a black dragon.  And stupid me was Satiated. Back down to
explore more and get hungry enough to eat a dragon.

Finally no longer Satiated, so back to Vlad's.  First was one of the
very few Wraith corpses.  Xp:16!  (still way too low). The black
dragon died quickly and after a long feast our hero felt firm.  I
think this was the last of the resistances he needed.

The rest of Vlad's was pretty typical.  The throne only gave our hero
a shock before disappearing.

On dlvl 40 our hero fell through a trap door and landed on Dlvl42,
which  was a level of the Wizard's tower!  Went up from there instead
of down.  Dlvl41 was also part of the Wizard's tower.  Then back to
dlvl40 where our hero came out in Orcus-town.  Orcus died pretty
quickly.  Unfortunately the death blow was also a lightning bolt that
blew up his nice iridium wand.

And for the first time I can recall on dlvl41 I encountered a
salamander outside of the Plane of Fire.  Just a weird game.

Dlvl 43 was the 3rd level of the Wizard's tower.  By this point I knew
I the game was close to an end.

Dlvl 44 was one of the fake towers.  Those snow boots in Vlad's tower
turned out to be quite useful.  This tower lead to the real tower.

Dlvl45 had the other fake tower.  There was also a magic trap, which
provided some fun and much needed charisma.

In these lower levels liches and R's quickly became a problem.
Nothing to be done but to hack and slash.  The hordes did occasionally
provide useful items like !oFH (very useful in that our hero still had
less than 200hp and only -22ac).

Then on dlvl47 I realized there was no downstairs and the floor was
too hard to dig into.  A brief search the VibSq was found!

So back up to buy the last bit of protection.  Then a plan would be
needed.  Ooops Orcus-town wasn't cleared yet.  It was here that
another blessed ?oGeno would have been extremely nice or a blessed
=oConflict.  Alas, no such luck our hero was hounded by a vicious
purple-L and its hordes.  It eventually summoned a Minotaur which had
to be teleported away to keep our hero alive.  Somehow our hero got
control of the upstairs, engraved the E-word, put on the =oLev, and
slowly killed the lich and the hordes. That was too close.

After recovering cleared out the rest of the town and then headed up
for the last bit of protection.

The priest was pretty useless.  So the next step was to get some ?oEA
and make my armor amazing and the the last item for my AK.  So bless
the extra magic lamp and get the wish and wish for a blessed ring of
conflict.  An  engagement ring?!?  I had two in the exploding bag!
Grrr.

Anyway next step was to improve the armor. Last real charge in the /
oWishing was used for a blessed magic marker.  I got enough ?oEA,?oEW,?
oCharging, and ?oGD to make me think the ascention run would be
possible.

Then I realized, for the Planes, I'd need conflict, free action, and
levitation, but could only wear two rings.  So back up to the castle
for the extra set of boots from Perseus.

Got Mjollnir up to +7.  Got a glows for a while message on the 100
arrows I had.  In retrospect, really should have used Magicbane as the
primary weapon and enchanted the arrows more too.

Anyway soon there was nothing else that could be done, so it was time
to wake the Wizard up.

The longbow proved very handy in killing all the ;.  The tower was
pretty easy.  I didn't bother collecting the gold, but probably should
have.

At the top of the Wizard's tower, I don't know what I was doing, but I
ate a piranha corpse while satiated.  BIG MISTAKE.

 This piranha corpse tastes terrible!  You choke over your food.--
More--

You die...

But wait...  Your medallion begins to glow!  You vomit ...--More--
You feel much better!
The medallion crumbles to dust!
You survived that attempt on your life.--More--
You stop eating the piranha corpse.

Yep I'm stupid.

Fortunately there was the "oLS from Vlad's which I promptly put on.

Then I woke up the wizard.  That's when I realized not having that /
oDeath really was going to be a problem.

But he still got the book.

Ran down to VibSq.  Got the ritual all out of order.  Also realized
some of the items were cursed.  Had to do it a 2nd time after blessing
everything, but eventually the staircase appeared.

The Sanctum wasn't much trouble.  There were a few !oGL and Wraith
corpses to be had.  Got up to Xp:19!   Not having a /oSDD was
annoying, but the real problem was the high priest.  He was impossible
to kill and Moloch kept throwing lightning bolts. Serious hp trouble.
Had to retreat a number of times.

But eventually our hero clutched the amulet in his hands.

Then it was Run Run Run.

Then the pesky wizard again.  There was something about double
trouble. I don't think I've seen that before.  There was two of him
now.  Monsters everywhere, time to whip out Magicbane and engrave the
E-word.  "Your Magicbane gets dull" WTF?!?  Oh I see some battle with
an L ended up with it cursed.  Grrrr.

This is where I realize I need to switch to Magicbane as the primary
weapon (after cleaning it with holy water a couple of times).

Only choice right now is to read a ?oTele.  While reading the scroll,
one Wizard escapes upstairs.  Must have been a cursed scroll as our
hero finds himself on Medusa's island (up about 10 or so levels from
where he was) with the other Wizard.

Eventually this 2nd Wizard is defeated.  And that's when it dawns on
me, I thought level teleport was blocked if you had the Amulet.  Oh I
see our hero doesn't have it any more.

Ok the amulet  is lost.  Magicbane needs to be fixed.  So more ?oEW
are needed.

I get the bright idea that maybe Venus can help with the enchantment
problem.  Although now that I think about it, I think Venus would only
uncurse and maybe rustproof it.

Anyway it was back up to the lowest level alter.  #offer and #pray a
lot.  Thanks to death drops, finally get Magicbane up to +0.

During all this time the Wizard never once appeared.  I guess as long
as he has the amulet he won't bother you.

Then I get the bright idea, use the last wish from the Castle Wand and
get a
/oDeath.

I also used a /oPoly to try and polymorph some scrolls into something
useful.

Back up to the alter for another #pray This time our hero got crowned.
While trying to get back to being able to pray, something dropped a
magic lamp.  Happy happy joy joy!  Then there was a wraith corpse, Xp:
20!

Do that and before entering Gehennom again, I post to the group about
the current crisis.

Logon again and start with the magic lamp.  Bless it and wish for a
magic marker.

Write some charging scrolls (for the /oDeath) and some enchant armor.
Get everything up to at least +4 and fixed except for the Boots of Lev
which were only at +2.

So now armed with a /oDeath, Magicbane and -40ac, our hero went
hunting for the wizard and the amulet. And on dlvl44 we found him,
with a horde of monsters no less!

Zap the death ray.  @#$@#$@# It misses.  I log out and come back the
next day.

Eventually the death ray hits.  Then the fight with the horde takes
quite a while, but at long last our hero recovers the Amulet.

Run Run Run. There were a few of the mysterious forces, but not nearly
as bad as other ascension runs I've done.  Wizard did appear some
more, but the /oDeath took care of him quickly.

Soon before I knew it, our hero was on dlvl1 ready to go upstairs.

I took another break here and came back the next day just to make sure
I was fresh and not going to do something stupid.

One more check on number of ?oGD and ?oCharge.  /oD is charged.  lots
of /oDigging.  Blessed =oConflict.  =oFA. extra =oFA.  Boots of Lev.
Ok ready!

PLANE OF EARTH - Yep the Wizard was there and died.  The Elfking and
the Minotaur also were quickly dispatched.

cursed ?oGD found the portal to be just a little north of where our
hero was. Didn't even need all the charges in just one /oDigging.

And here's where I made my first mistake.  I forgot to put on the
boots of Lev.
PLANE OF AIR - Scramble to put the boots of Lev on.  Confused blessed ?
oGD found the portal more or less of a straight line on the other side
of the map.

Avoiding the Air Elementals proved to be a lot easier than usual. Our
hero only got engluphed once.  Fortunately Magicbane scared him and he
expelled our hero three steps from the portal.

PLANE OF FIRE - Take out a ?oGD.  It burns to a crisp.  At first I
thought that meant I lost it, but it appeared in the inventory.
Confused ?oGD again and the portal just a few steps due West.  Run!

PLANE OF WATER - I hate this one.  My newest strategy  is to read a
confused ?oGD then just sit in my bubble until the portal comes to
me.  Nothing else seems to work.  Eventually we move on to the next
level.

ASTRAL PLANE - Our hero arrived between the center and Eastern
alters.  Telepathy showed Death guarding the Eastern Alter, so our
hero headed for the center alter.

In spite of a horde of monsters around us, something was ignoring
conflict and hitting our hero.  Had to take off the boots of lev,
engrave the E-word. Meanwhile hp dropped to less than half.  Some of
the horde kills each other and our hero makes a break for the
opening.

In many ways right now, it was good L's never got geno.  Their hordes
were great protection and killed almost everything dangerous.

Famine was dead before we got to him.  He revived and was killed
again.  Got to the center alter, it was the wrong one.  Famine revived
again. This time our hero's  /oDeath took care of him.

Next was to head for the Western alter.  On the way we found an Amulet
of Yendor on the ground.  I still had the real thing in the inventory
though.  Massive confusion ensued.  Assuming the one named "the real
thing" was the right one, our hero ignored the one on the ground.

The last charge on the /oD was used on Pestilence.  Took a few seconds
to recharge the wand and continued the trek to the Western alter.

Pestilence revived and was quickly killed by the horde.

Finally arrived at the alter.  It was the correct one! #offered the
Amulet, had the invisible choir, etc.

Actually had an uncursed dilithium crystal

